[150,1017,1018,1019,1022,1023,1026,1027,1029],{},"On Windows, ",[181,1020,1021],{},"taskkill"," sends a termination that does ",[241,1024,1025],{},"not"," always reach a\nconsole process as ",[181,1028,1001],{}," — the reliable paths are Ctrl+C \u002F Ctrl+Break.",[261,1031,1033],{"id":1032},"what-the-daemon-does-on-start","What the daemon does on start",[1035,1036,1037,1048,1054,1065],"ol",{},[1038,1039,1040,1041,1043,1044,1047],"li",{},"Resolves the storage (",[181,1042,448],{},"); a non-sqlite storage validates its\nconnstring env ",[241,1045,1046],{},"before"," anything starts (missing env → fail-fast).",[1038,1049,1050,1051,1053],{},"Syncs ",[181,1052,413],{}," into storage (desired state; removed tasks get disabled).",[1038,1055,1056,1057,1060,1061,1064],{},"Validates every task's runner is registered — a missing runner ",[241,1058,1059],{},"aborts startup",":\n",[181,1062,1063],{},"task \"greet\": runner \"custom\" not implemented in this build (registered: http, docker)",".",[1038,1066,1067,1068,1071,1072,874,1074,1076],{},"Starts the tick loop (fires due tasks), the watchdog (reaps zombie locks), the\npoll loop (async ",[181,1069,1070],{},"accepted"," runs), and the retention loop (hourly sweep of\nterminal runs past their TTL — ",[181,1073,505],{},[181,1075,534],{},").",[261,1078,527],{"id":1079},"retention",[150,1081,1082,1083,874,1086,874,1089,1092,1093,1095],{},"Terminal runs (",[181,1084,1085],{},"succeeded",[181,1087,1088],{},"failed",[181,1090,1091],{},"cancelled",") are pruned by the retention\nloop (hourly) once they're past their class TTL, measured from ",[181,1094,514],{},":",[1097,1098,1099,1111],"ul",{},[1038,1100,1101,1103,1104,1106,1107,1110],{},[181,1102,543],{}," runs → ",[181,1105,534],{}," (default ",[241,1108,1109],{},"24 h",");",[1038,1112,1113,1114,1106,1116,1076],{},"regular runs → ",[181,1115,505],{},[241,1117,1118],{},"30 d",[150,1120,1121,1122,1127,1128,1131,1132,1134,1135,1138],{},"Set the TTL to ",[241,1123,1124,1126],{},[181,1125,520],{}," to turn retention off for that class"," — run history is kept\nforever. This is the archive mode for deployments that migrate legacy history\ninto sched (books: migrated ",[181,1129,1130],{},"task_runs"," carry old ",[181,1133,514],{}," timestamps, and\nwith the 30 d default the first hourly pass would silently prune everything\nolder than a month — ",[181,1136,1137],{},"--retention-ttl 0 --temporary-retention-ttl 0"," keeps the\narchive).",[236,1140,1141],{},[150,1142,1143,1144,1146],{},"Note: ",[181,1145,520],{}," was added in daemon 0.11.0. Earlier versions had no way to disable\nretention — a migration onto the 30 d default pruned aged history.",[261,1148,1150],{"id":1149},"example","Example",[266,1152,1154],{"className":268,"code":1153,"language":270,"meta":271,"style":271},"SCHED_ADMIN_KEY=dev-key schedd \\\n  --tasks tasks.json \\\n  --db sched.db \\\n  --admin-port 8080\n",[181,1155,1156,1171,1180,1190],{"__ignoreMap":271},[275,1157,1158,1160,1162,1165,1167],{"class":277,"line":278},[275,1159,666],{"class":943},[275,1161,946],{"class":306},[275,1163,1164],{"class":288},"dev-key",[275,1166,952],{"class":281},[275,1168,1170],{"class":1169},"se3Ec"," \\\n",[275,1172,1173,1176,1178],{"class":277,"line":21},[275,1174,1175],{"class":955},"  --tasks",[275,1177,959],{"class":288},[275,1179,1170],{"class":1169},[275,1181,1182,1185,1188],{"class":277,"line":332},[275,1183,1184],{"class":955},"  --db",[275,1186,1187],{"class":288}," sched.db",[275,1189,1170],{"class":1169},[275,1191,1192,1195],{"class":277,"line":363},[275,1193,1194],{"class":955},"  --admin-port",[275,1196,1198],{"class":1197},"s7CZa"," 8080\n",[150,1200,1201,1202,1207,1208,1211,1212,215,1215,1218,1219,1222],{},"Then the admin api answers on ",[524,1203,1204],{"href":1204,"rel":1205},"http:\u002F\u002F127.0.0.1:8080\u002Fapi\u002F",[1206],"nofollow","*. The operator CLI\n(",[181,1209,1210],{},"sched status --admin-url http:\u002F\u002F127.0.0.1:8080\u002Fapi",") and the web UI\n(",[181,1213,1214],{},"npx @schedjs\u002Fui",[181,1216,1217],{},"sched-ui serve --proxy http:\u002F\u002F127.0.0.1:8080",", see\n",[524,1220,121],{"href":1221},"ui",") both speak to it.",[223,1224],{},[226,1226,1228,1229],{"id":1227},"operator-cli-sched","Operator CLI — ",[181,1230,198],{},[150,1232,1233,1235,1236,1239,1240,1243,1244,1247],{},[181,1234,203],{}," — a thin projection of the admin REST API (",[524,1237,117],{"href":1238},"admin-api","):\nstatus, runs, tasks, schedules, trigger, pause\u002Fresume. Zero dependencies\n(",[181,1241,1242],{},"node:fetch"," only); the daemon stays the single owner of state. Machine output\nis ",[181,1245,1246],{},"--json","; tables are for TTY eyes only.",[261,1249,1251],{"id":1250},"install","Install",[266,1253,1255],{"className":268,"code":1254,"language":270,"meta":271,"style":271},"npm install -g @schedjs\u002Fcli\n",[181,1256,1257],{"__ignoreMap":271},[275,1258,1259,1262,1265,1268],{"class":277,"line":278},[275,1260,1261],{"class":281},"npm",[275,1263,1264],{"class":288}," install",[275,1266,1267],{"class":955}," -g",[275,1269,1270],{"class":288}," @schedjs\u002Fcli\n",[261,1272,264],{"id":1273},"usage-1",[266,1275,1278],{"className":1276,"code":1277,"language":910,"meta":271},[908],"sched \u003Ccommand> [args] [--admin-url URL] [--api-key KEY] [--json]\n\nCommands:\n  status                   daemon health + queue state + task\u002Fschedule\u002Frun counts\n  runs [--task T] [--status S] [--limit N] [--offset N]\n       [--since TIME] [--until TIME] [--runner R]\n  cancel \u003Cid...>           bulk-cancel runs (partial result; exit 1 on any failure)\n  retry \u003Cid...>            bulk-retry finished runs (partial result; exit 1 on any failure)\n  tasks\n  schedules\n  trigger \u003Ctask> [--data JSON]\n  pause \u003Ctask> | pause --schedule \u003Cid>\n  resume \u003Ctask> | resume --schedule \u003Cid>\n  check-worker \u003Curl> [--api-key KEY] [--timeout SECONDS]\n",[181,1279,1277],{"__ignoreMap":271},[150,1281,1282,1285,1286,756,1289,756,1292,756,1295,1298,1299,874,1302,1305,1306,1309,1310,932,1312,1314,1315,1318,1319,1322,1323,756,1326,756,1329,756,1332,1335,1336,1339,1340,923,1344,1346,1347,1351,1352,1355],{},[181,1283,1284],{},"runs"," filters: ",[181,1287,1288],{},"task",[181,1290,1291],{},"status",[181,1293,1294],{},"limit",[181,1296,1297],{},"offset"," plus the R4 window\n",[181,1300,1301],{},"--since",[181,1303,1304],{},"--until"," and the exact ",[181,1307,1308],{},"--runner"," match. ",[181,1311,1301],{},[181,1313,1304],{},"\naccept ",[241,1316,1317],{},"ISO-8601"," or a ",[241,1320,1321],{},"relative form"," — ",[181,1324,1325],{},"30m",[181,1327,1328],{},"24h",[181,1330,1331],{},"7d",[181,1333,1334],{},"2w"," (\"that\nlong ago\"); the relative form is resolved by the CLI, and the admin API always\nreceives ISO-8601. The window is on ",[181,1337,1338],{},"startedAt",", both bounds inclusive (see\n",[524,1341,1343],{"href":1342},"runs#filtering-run-history","Runs → Filtering",[181,1345,1246],{}," echoes the ",[1348,1349,1350],"em",{},"resolved","\nfilter, so ",[181,1353,1354],{},"--since 24h"," shows the exact ISO bound that was queried.",[150,1357,1358],{},"Global flags:",[154,1360,1361,1374],{},[157,1362,1363],{},[160,1364,1365,1367,1370,1372],{},[163,1366,393],{},[163,1368,1369],{},"Env",[163,1371,396],{},[163,1373,399],{},[173,1375,1376,1400,1416,1429],{},[160,1377,1378,1383,1388,1393],{},[178,1379,1380],{},[181,1381,1382],{},"--admin-url URL",[178,1384,1385],{},[181,1386,1387],{},"SCHED_ADMIN_URL",[178,1389,1390],{},[181,1391,1392],{},"http:\u002F\u002F127.0.0.1:8080\u002Fapi",[178,1394,1395,1396,1399],{},"Admin API base — note the ",[181,1397,1398],{},"\u002Fapi"," mount point is already included",[160,1401,1402,1407,1411,1413],{},[178,1403,1404],{},[181,1405,1406],{},"--api-key KEY",[178,1408,1409],{},[181,1410,666],{},[178,1412,620],{},[178,1414,1415],{},"Bearer key for the admin API",[160,1417,1418,1422,1424,1426],{},[178,1419,1420],{},[181,1421,1246],{},[178,1423,620],{},[178,1425,620],{},[178,1427,1428],{},"Stable machine-readable JSON contract",[160,1430,1431,1445,1447,1449],{},[178,1432,1433,874,1436,756,1439,874,1442],{},[181,1434,1435],{},"-h",[181,1437,1438],{},"--help",[181,1440,1441],{},"-v",[181,1443,1444],{},"--version",[178,1446,620],{},[178,1448,620],{},[178,1450,1451],{},"Help \u002F version",[150,1453,1454,1455,1457,1458,1461,1462,1465],{},"Exit codes: ",[241,1456,520],{}," ok \u002F ",[241,1459,1460],{},"1"," api·network·data error \u002F ",[241,1463,1464],{},"2"," usage.",[150,1467,1468,874,1471,1474,1475,1478,1479,1482,1483,1486,1487,1489,1490,1492],{},[181,1469,1470],{},"cancel",[181,1472,1473],{},"retry"," take one or more run ids and return a ",[241,1476,1477],{},"partial result","\n(",[181,1480,1481],{},"{ ok, failed }",", reason ∈ ",[181,1484,1485],{},"not-found | already-terminal | not-cancellable",").\nExit code ",[241,1488,1460],{}," whenever at least one id failed, ",[241,1491,520],{}," only on a fully clean\nbatch — so a partial batch never reads as success to a shell.",[150,1494,1495,1498,1499,1501,1502,1505],{},[181,1496,1497],{},"--api-key"," before the command is the admin key; after ",[181,1500,209],{}," it is the\n",[1348,1503,1504],{},"worker's"," key (a different secret — see below).",[261,1507,1509],{"id":1508},"examples","Examples",[266,1511,1513],{"className":268,"code":1512,"language":270,"meta":271,"style":271},"sched status                                   # is my daemon alive? queue paused? next runs?\nsched runs --status failed --limit 20 --json   # failed runs as JSON\nsched runs --since 24h --until 2h --runner docker   # what fell over in the last 22 hours, docker only\nsched cancel r-1 r-2 r-3                       # bulk-cancel a mixed batch\nsched trigger publish-video --data '{\"videoId\":\"v-42\"}'\nsched pause --schedule channel-ada             # pause one channel's schedule, not the task\nsched resume sync-channel-stats\n",[181,1514,1515,1526,1551,1578,1597,1621,1638],{"__ign